<document><languages><language><identifier lang="ident latin">kaw</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Old Javanese</name><script><identifier lang="ident latin">kawi</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Kawi</name></script></language><language><identifier lang="ident latin">san</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Sanskrit</name><script><identifier lang="ident latin">kawi</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Kawi</name></script></language></languages><scripts><script><identifier lang="ident latin">kawi</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Kawi</name><language><identifier lang="ident latin">kaw</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Old Javanese</name></language><language><identifier lang="ident latin">san</identifier><name lang="eng latin">Sanskrit</name></language></script></scripts><title lang="eng latin">Alasantan</title><editor><name lang="eng latin">Eko Bastiawan</name><identifier lang="ident latin">ekba</identifier></editor><editor><name lang="eng latin">Arlo Griffiths</name><identifier lang="ident latin">argr</identifier></editor><hand><para lang="eng latin">The use of layar is normally in Indian mode, but Indonesian mode is also found at least once (and marked with = as per TG 3.8.8).</para><para lang="eng latin">The lowest level punctuation sign, provisionally represented here by ",", takes the shape of a median dot.</para></hand><edition><head lang="eng latin">Edition</head><physical><page><head><npage break="true" phantom="false" significant="true"><span tip="Page start" lang="zxx latin">⟨Page 1r⟩</span><span class="fw" tip="Foliation" lang="zxx latin">⟨left: <!--space--><span class="fw-contents"><span class="num" lang="san kawi">1</span></span>⟩</span></npage></head><line lang="kaw kawi"><nline break="true" phantom="false" significant="true"><span tip="Line start" lang="zxx latin">⟨1r1⟩</span><!--space--> </nline><ncell break="true" phantom="true" significant="true"/><split><display><span tip="Punctuation symbol: double vertical bar with a hook on top of one or both bars" class="symbol" lang="san kawi">||</span></display><search lang="san kawi">■</search></split><!--space--> <split><display><span tip="Punctuation symbol: circle with a concentric dot, Cambodian “Chicken eye”" class="symbol" lang="san kawi">◯</span></display><search lang="san kawi">■</search></split><!--space--> <split><display><span tip="Punctuation symbol: double vertical bar with a hook on top of one or both bars" class="symbol" lang="san kawi">||</span></display><search lang="san kawi">■</search></split><!--space--> namo ’stu ṣad-vināyakāya <!--space--><split><display><span tip="Punctuation symbol: double vertical bar with a hook on top of one or both bars" class="symbol" lang="san kawi">||</span></display><search lang="san kawi">■</search></split><!--space--> <split><display><span tip="Punctuation symbol: small circle (noticeably smaller than a typical character body), placed at median height; Cambodian “Chicken egg”" class="symbol" lang="san kawi">◯</span></display><search lang="san kawi">■</search></split><!--space--> <split><display><span tip="Punctuation symbol: double vertical bar with a hook on top of one or both bars" class="symbol" lang="san kawi">||</span></display><search lang="san kawi">■</search></split><!--space--> svastī śaka-varṣātīta <!--space--><span class="num" lang="kaw kawi">861</span><!--space--> bhadravāda-māsa, tithi pañcami kr̥ṣṇa-pakṣa, <!--space--><span class="abbr" tip="Abbreviated text" lang="kaw kawi">vā</span>, <!--space--><span class="abbr" tip="Abbreviated text" lang="kaw kawi">pa</span>, <!--space--><span class="abbr" tip="Abbreviated text" lang="kaw kawi">śu</span>, vāra, Aśvinī-nakṣatra, Aśvī-devatā, vi<span tip="Hyphen break" lang="zxx latin">-</span></line><line lang="kaw kawi"><nline break="false" phantom="false" significant="true"><span tip="Line start" lang="zxx latin">⟨1r2⟩</span><!--space--> </nline><ncell break="false" phantom="true" significant="true"/>ṣkambha-yoga, Irikā divasani Ājñā śrī mahārāja <!--space--><span